{"id":"9b622e4c-9dfa-490a-9b03-8692633a1a05","object":"chat.completion","created":1784980325,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"import math\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    # Input fields\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    idf = case['idf']\\n    vector = case['vector']\\n    \\n    n_rows = len(matrix)\\n    n_cols = len(idf)\\n    \\n    # Step 1: Scale each column by its IDF\\n    X_scaled = [[0.0] * n_cols for _ in range(n_rows)]\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        for j in range(n_cols):\\n            X_scaled[i][j] = matrix[i][j] * idf[j]\\n    \\n    # Step 2: Compute row degrees (squared norm) with positive floor\\n    EPS = 1e-10\\n    degrees = []\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        sq_norm = sum(x * x for x in X_scaled[i])\\n        if sq_norm < EPS:\\n            sq_norm = EPS\\n        degrees.append(sq_norm)\\n    \\n    # Step 3: Inverse square-root scaling of input vector\\n    v_scaled = [vector[i] / math.sqrt(degrees[i]) for i in range(n_rows)]\\n    \\n    # Step 4: First product: t = X_scaled^T * v_scaled (size n_cols)\\n    t = [0.0] * n_cols\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        for j in range(n_cols):\\n            t[j] += X_scaled[i][j] * v_scaled[i]\\n    \\n    # Step 5: Second product: u = X_scaled * t (size n_rows)\\n    u = [0.0] * n_rows\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        for j in range(n_cols):\\n            u[i] += X_scaled[i][j] * t[j]\\n    \\n    # Step 6: Rescale rows: apply D^{-1/2} again\\n    result = [u[i] / math.sqrt(degrees[i]) for i in range(n_rows)]\\n    \\n    # Round to 8 decimal places for deterministic output\\n    degree_out = [round(d, 8) for d in degrees]\\n    result_out = [round(r, 8) for r in result]\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'degree': degree_out,\\n        'result': result_out\\n    }\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the problem: It's a programming task for a function `solve(case)` that takes a payload (ob